    "abstract": "Illustrated parts figure for the aft cargo compartment ceiling and sidewall lining, the panel latches, the restraint decor panels and the compartment lighting in both the fluorescent and solid state standards.",
    "sections": {
      "purpose": "This figure identifies the aft cargo compartment lining panels, their latches and standoff brackets, and the compartment lighting assemblies, for all ZEPHYR-22 family aircraft.",
      "figure_note": "The view is taken looking forward from the aft bulkhead with the ceiling panels lowered. Items 60 and 60A are the two lighting standards; the solid state item is driven from the cabin intercommunication system and cannot be fitted to a compartment that still has fluorescent ballasts. The latch at item 20 is common to both standards, but the deeper standoff bracket required by the upgraded acoustic blanket is a different length and is called out separately on sheet 2."
    },
